<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert 0 <= index && index <= \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index <= i && i < \old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null ? \old(this.get(i+1)) == null : this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))));</code>

This assertion ensures that if the `index` is within the valid range (from 0 to the size of the list inclusive), then for every valid index `i` starting from `index` up to the old size of the list minus one, the element at position `i` in the new list is either `null` if the element at position `i+1` in the old list was `null`, or it is equal to the element at position `i+1` in the old list.
